          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Two Variables, One Line"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.841,
            0.071,
            0.881,
            0.087
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "105"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.11,
            0.881,
            0.148
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In general, a pair of linear equations in two variables x and y can be written as:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.149,
            0.881,
            0.207
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a_{1}x + b_{1}y + c_{1} = 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a_{2}x + b_{2}y + c_{2} = 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , where "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a_{1}, b_{1}, c_{1}, a_{2}, b_{2}, c_{2}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " are all real numbers, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a _ { \\mathrm { { _ 1 } } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "b _ { 1 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " are not both zero, and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a _ { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "b _ { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " are not both zero."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "doc_title",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.365,
            0.249,
            0.631,
            0.279
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Exercise Set 13.4"
            }
          ],
          "level": 1
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.292,
            0.881,
            0.333
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Given below are some everyday situations. Construct a pair of linear equations in two variables for each situation:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.138,
            0.336,
            0.882,
            0.414
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. On two different days a family buys movie tickets and snack boxes. Let the cost of one movie ticket be ₹x and the cost of one snack box be ₹y. Frame a pair of linear equations in x and y to represent the following situations:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.196,
            0.413,
            0.881,
            0.451
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) On the first day, the family buys 2 movie tickets and 3 snack boxes for ₹850."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.19,
            0.451,
            0.881,
            0.491
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) On the second day, the family buys 4 movie tickets and 1 snack box for ₹1100."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.138,
            0.495,
            0.882,
            0.573
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. Two friends, Sahil and Meena, travelled by taxi. Let the fixed charge for one taxi trip be ₹x and the additional charge per kilometre be ₹y. Frame a pair of linear equations in x and y to represent the following situation:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.197,
            0.572,
            0.769,
            0.591
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) Sahil travelled 6 km and paid a total fare of ₹122."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.19,
            0.591,
            0.786,
            0.611
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) Meena travelled 8 km and paid a total fare of ₹160."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.138,
            0.616,
            0.883,
            0.733
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. In a sports meet, tickets for adults cost ₹150 each and tickets for children cost ₹100 each. A total of 200 people attended the meet, and the total amount collected from ticket sales was ₹25,000. (Let the number of adult tickets sold be x and the number of children’s tickets sold be y.) Frame a pair of linear equations in x and y to represent this situation."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.757,
            0.875,
            0.78
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "13.5 Finding Solutions to a Pair of Linear Equations"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.79,
            0.882,
            0.87
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We have already seen how to solve a linear equation in a single variable. In order to find the solution of a pair of linear equations, we need to think of methods by which we can reduce the pair to a linear equation in one variable. In this section we shall study two methods."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
